## PROJECT DOCUMENTATION & CONTEXT SYSTEM

All project documentation, including coding standards, workflow guidelines, and this rules file itself, will be stored in the project root directory.  The main documentation will be in markdown format.  New versions of this file will be tracked with timestamps in filenames (e.g., `ai_coding_assistant_rules_2025-10-27.md`).  Version updates to the Prisma schema are documented in the `README.md` file within the `document-processing` directory. The `schema-extension.sql` file contains PostgreSQL-specific extensions, functions, and policies that complement the Prisma schema.  Comprehensive documentation for Prisma setup and usage, including context7 MCP, should be added to the `document-processing` directory.  This documentation should follow a step-by-step approach, including planning and pseudocode stages.  The documentation should also include details about existing database structure and the relevant files (e.g., `index.ts`, `schema.prisma`, `schema-extension.sql`).


